    "result_text": "All tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response.\n\n**Change made** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: Added `@jakarta.validation.constraints.PastOrPresent` to the `registrationDate` field of the `OwnerFields` schema (via `x-field-extra-annotation`), and updated its description to note the rejection.\n\nThis is the idiomatic Spring Bean Validation approach already used throughout this spec (`@NotBlank`, `@Email`, `@PostcodeValidation`, etc.). The annotation is applied to the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, and because the create endpoint already validates the request body, a future date now triggers a `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to **400 Bad Request**. `PastOrPresent` allows today (the server date) and null (field is optional), so existing create flows are unaffected \u2014 only strictly-future dates are rejected.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `2999-01-01`) now passes, and the full suite is green.",
