        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- The project generates its DTOs from `openapi.yml` via openapi-generator, and `x-field-extra-annotation` is the established, repo-wide mechanism for attaching Bean Validation constraints to generated fields (`@NotBlank`, `@Email`, and even a custom `@PetAgeValidation` all use it). Adding `@PastOrPresent` to `registrationDate` follows that exact convention \u2014 I confirmed it generates onto `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto` alongside the siblings.\n- The constraint lives in the right unit: on the schema field itself, so validation is declared once at the model and enforced by the standard Spring MVC `@Valid` pipeline (which yields the 400 the spec wants). No new catch-all class, no controller/service logic duplicating the check.\n- `@PastOrPresent` is the precise semantic match for \"reject a date later than the server date\" (future rejected, today allowed), and the schema `description` was updated in step with the behavior, keeping the contract and docs coherent.\n\nNo structural improvements needed."
